$ w --why 3 coffees in mg of caffeine

  ◆ interpretation
  │ 3 × coffee(95 mg caffeine)  →  mg of caffeine

  ◆ result
  │ 285 mg

  ◆ other units
  │ 0.285 g  ·  0.01005 oz  ·  2.85×10⁻⁴ kg

  ◆ sources
  │ coffee · caffeine  USDA FoodData Central, Beverages, coffee, brewed,
  │   prepared with tap water: 40 mg caffeine and 1 kcal per 100 g; an 8 fl oz
  │   cup weighs 237 g
  │ mg (g)             BIPM SI Brochure (9th ed., 2019), §2.3.1, Table 2
  │   (kilogram is the base unit; prefixes attach to gram, §3)

  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── W74
